Feature 1 — Create Account

Ask for:

Customer name
Initial deposit

Rules:

Name cannot be empty.
Initial deposit cannot be negative.
Generate a unique account number.
Balance starts with the initial deposit.
Add a history entry:
"Account created with $500"
Feature 2 — Deposit

Ask for:

Account number
Amount

Rules:

Account must exist.
Deposit must be greater than 0.
Increase balance.
Record the transaction.

Example history:

Deposited $100
Feature 3 — Withdraw

Ask for:

Account number
Amount

Rules:

Account exists.
Amount > 0.
Cannot withdraw more than the balance.
Update balance.
Save transaction.

Example:

Withdrew $75
Feature 4 — Transfer

Ask for:

Sender account
Receiver account
Amount

Rules:

Both accounts exist.
Cannot transfer to the same account.
Enough balance.
Update both balances.
Record the transfer in both histories.

Example:

Sender:

Transferred $100 to account 1002

Receiver:

Received $100 from account 1001
Feature 5 — View Account

Display:

Account Number: 1001
Owner: Michael
Balance: $425.50
Feature 6 — View All Accounts

Example:

1001 - Michael - $425.50


1002 - Sarah - $985.00


1003 - John - $12.00
Feature 7 — Transaction History

Ask for an account number.

Display every transaction.

Example:

Account created with $500


Deposited $200


Transferred $50 to account 1002


Withdrew $25
Feature 8 — Save Accounts

Save everything to a JSON file.

Suggested filename:

accounts.json

Use the json module instead of writing plain text. This preserves the full account structure.

Feature 9 — Load Accounts

When selected, load data from accounts.json.

If the file doesn't exist:

No saved accounts found.

The program should continue running instead of crashing.

Feature 10 — Exit

Before exiting:

Would you like to save first? (Y/N)
Validation Requirements

Your program should gracefully handle:

Empty names
Invalid account numbers
Negative deposits
Negative withdrawals
Deposits of zero
Withdrawals of zero
Insufficient funds
Transfers to the same account
Non-numeric input where numbers are expected
Missing JSON file
Corrupted JSON file (optional bonus)

The program should never crash because of user input.

Recommended Functions

Try to write one function per responsibility, for example:

create_account()
deposit()
withdraw()
transfer()
view_account()
view_all_accounts()
show_history()
save_accounts()
load_accounts()
generate_account_number()
find_account()
Extra Challenge (Optional)

If you finish the core features, try adding:

Delete an account (only if the balance is $0).
Search accounts by customer name.
Display the bank's total assets (sum of all balances).
Show the top 5 accounts with the highest balances.
Charge a monthly maintenance fee to all accounts.
Calculate and apply interest to savings accounts.
Rules

To get the most out of this exercise, challenge yourself with these constraints:

✅ Use only programming fundamentals (functions, loops, dictionaries, lists, conditionals, exceptions, file handling).
❌ Don't use classes or object-oriented programming yet.
❌ Don't use external libraries beyond Python's standard library (such as json).

If you can complete this project cleanly with solid validation and program logic, you'll have a very strong grasp of Python fundamentals and be well prepared to move on to object-oriented programming and more advanced projects.